<http://data.silknow.org/object/52ab5c09-f7d5-3415-ace8-b63e6eebdb9a/observation/3>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The layout of borders on bag faces is often more complex than it is on floor carpets.  Sometimes, as in this example, one border runs along the bottom and part of the way up each side, while the others expand to form a T-shape. There are sometimes extra borders, such as the narrow one along the upper edge. Perhaps because bag faces are relatively small, time was taken to include many small details. Small amounts of light purple silk have been used in the pile."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/52ab5c09-f7d5-3415-ace8-b63e6eebdb9a> .

<https://sws.geonames.org/130758/>
        a       ecrm:E53_Place .

